WEBVTT

00:00.033 --> 00:29.955
The Witness of a Brief Moment.

00:00.837 --> 00:02.581
Who is the culprit behind the explosion?

00:02.839 --> 00:04.799
The witness lost her sight.

00:04.800 --> 00:07.468
See the miraculous operation to bring her sight back.

00:07.469 --> 00:09.470
Make sure to list all suspects!

00:09.471 --> 00:10.679
I saw him.

00:10.680 --> 00:12.515
I have four suspects in custody.

00:12.673 --> 00:14.682
He came to the train tracks.

00:14.684 --> 00:16.393
There's no way to treat her.

00:16.394 --> 00:18.938
Just one minute will do, as long as
we can show her the suspects!

00:19.067 --> 00:20.606
But what about the patient?

00:20.607 --> 00:21.649
Open your eye slowly.

00:21.650 --> 00:24.777
Is the man you saw one of these men?

00:25.695 --> 00:26.403
That's the man!

00:26.653 --> 00:29.813
Black Jack, Today's Karte - The Witness of a Brief Moment.

00:30.082 --> 00:36.705
I'm going to fly to where you are.

00:30.082 --> 00:36.705
kimi no moto e tonde yuku yo

00:37.040 --> 00:44.046
I know I can spread my wings when I want to see you.

00:37.040 --> 00:44.046
aitai toki tsubasa hiraku

00:44.631 --> 00:47.716
Nobody knows

00:44.631 --> 00:47.716
dara nimo wakaranai

00:48.135 --> 00:51.554
when a miracle might occur,

00:48.135 --> 00:51.554
kiseki wa itsu okiru?

00:51.555 --> 00:57.977
but it feels like my wish is finally coming true.

00:51.555 --> 00:57.977
nozomi wa kanaeraresou de

00:57.978 --> 01:04.775
Because there's only one place I want to go,

00:57.978 --> 01:04.775
mukau basho wa hitotsu shika nai kara

01:04.776 --> 01:08.028
iro asenai omoi yosete

01:04.776 --> 01:08.028
I gather my feelings whose colors never fade,

01:08.029 --> 01:11.574
and now it seems I'm dreaming.

01:08.029 --> 01:11.574
saa Dreaming now

01:12.159 --> 01:15.494
I'm living for your sake?

01:12.159 --> 01:15.494
kimi no tame ni iketeru

01:15.495 --> 01:18.664
I will be your strength,

01:15.495 --> 01:18.664
donna chikara nimo naru

01:18.957 --> 01:21.876
no matter how far apart we are.

01:18.957 --> 01:21.876
Far away Far away harukana

01:21.877 --> 01:25.671
So Freedom. So Freedom.

01:25.797 --> 01:29.258
I will send you

01:25.797 --> 01:29.258
kimi no tame no okurou

01:29.259 --> 01:32.511
the beautiful blossom of this flower.

01:29.259 --> 01:32.511
kirei ni saita hana wo

01:32.679 --> 01:35.598
So let's look for shooting stars.

01:32.679 --> 01:35.598
Shooting Star Shooting Star sagasou

01:35.599 --> 01:39.602
So Freedom. So Freedom.

02:17.849 --> 02:19.141
Come on, Pinoco. Hurry up.

02:19.142 --> 02:19.767
Let's go.

02:19.865 --> 02:21.977
Hang on a minute.

02:21.978 --> 02:26.732
I really can't decide which one to get.

02:28.355 --> 02:31.001
Good grief, you've been thinking about it long enough!

02:43.667 --> 02:45.000
Coffee, please.

02:45.025 --> 02:45.325
Okay.

02:47.170 --> 02:48.629
It will be ¥120.

02:57.668 --> 02:58.847
This one?

03:00.100 --> 03:02.434
It will be ¥240.

03:04.257 --> 03:07.267
Originally "The Witness" by Tezuka Osamu

03:04.257 --> 03:07.267
The Witness of a Brief Moment

03:07.410 --> 03:09.350
Beef Overload

03:13.876 --> 03:17.144
New Treasure Island
Coming to Theaters

03:15.031 --> 03:16.443
Hang on.

03:16.503 --> 03:17.134
What?

03:17.158 --> 03:20.494
I'll go exchange this for the other one.

03:20.495 --> 03:22.371
Hey, we don't have much time.

03:22.372 --> 03:24.329
I'll be right back!

04:23.099 --> 04:25.142
Wait up, Doc!

04:26.662 --> 04:27.770
This is...

04:32.359 --> 04:35.093
Wh-What happened here?

04:36.881 --> 04:38.212
There was an explosion.

04:38.573 --> 04:41.325
I don't know what caused it, but something exploded.

04:41.701 --> 04:43.077
An explosion?!

04:43.078 --> 04:44.164
What?

04:44.829 --> 04:46.080
Something exploded!

04:47.082 --> 04:48.864
This is terrible!

04:51.544 --> 04:53.212
Hello, emergency?

04:53.213 --> 04:54.254
There was an explosion at the train station.

04:54.687 --> 04:55.506
It's an accident.

04:55.548 --> 04:57.390
It's huge! It's a disaster!

05:33.878 --> 05:35.129
Thank you for coming.

05:35.244 --> 05:36.255
What's the situation?

05:36.256 --> 05:39.133
Sir, it seems an explosive device was planted here.

05:39.134 --> 05:40.391
The number of casualties is unknown.

05:40.760 --> 05:44.847
We're currently transferring all the
injured victims to area hospitals.

05:48.268 --> 05:49.268
Is that...

05:49.269 --> 05:53.171
He said he's a doctor, so we told him to help with first aid.

05:53.356 --> 05:57.359
But the ambulance crews have arrived,
so we can relieve him now.

05:57.360 --> 05:58.874
Hey, that's enough.

05:59.112 --> 06:01.211
You can leave the rest to the paramedics and go.

06:01.489 --> 06:04.359
This victim will definitely die if we move him now.

06:04.868 --> 06:08.537
Chase us away by force if that's what you want.

06:09.456 --> 06:10.581
Why...

06:10.606 --> 06:11.026
Hey!

06:11.100 --> 06:11.613
Wait

06:12.125 --> 06:14.789
I think that's Dr. Black Jack.

06:14.997 --> 06:15.901
He is?

06:16.249 --> 06:18.083
Send a few paramedics to assist him.

06:18.084 --> 06:18.685
What?

06:18.960 --> 06:21.795
Get him help if he needs it!

06:21.845 --> 06:22.461
Sir!

06:22.713 --> 06:23.922
Call the forensics team to the scene!

06:24.465 --> 06:26.758
Form a cordon with a twenty kilometer radius,
and set up check points.

06:26.759 --> 06:31.430
Anyone who's free should start searching for witnesses,
and make sure to list all suspects!

06:31.739 --> 06:33.723
Don't miss a single suspect!

06:33.777 --> 06:34.219
Sir!

06:37.311 --> 06:42.023
This is a criminal incident of unprecedented cruelty.

06:42.650 --> 06:45.318
In order to prevent this from ever happening again,

06:45.319 --> 06:47.571
arresting the culprit is the highest priority.

06:47.572 --> 06:49.030
Now, explain the situation.

06:49.031 --> 06:49.865
Yes, sir.

06:50.616 --> 06:52.409
The casualty count stands at twenty-eight.

06:52.410 --> 06:56.336
It is believed that an explosive device set in a suitcase
was triggered from a remote location.

06:56.664 --> 06:59.499
The bomb was a high-energy plastic explosive.

06:59.500 --> 07:02.127
The forensics team is looking for further details.

07:02.128 --> 07:06.506
As the result of interviews and other investigation,
we currently have four suspects in custody.

07:06.507 --> 07:10.010
All suspects were present at the crime
scene at the time of the explosion.

07:10.470 --> 07:14.055
Suwa Michihiko. Age 42. TV producer.

07:10.470 --> 07:14.055
Name Suwa Michihiko
Age 42
Occupation TV Station Producer

07:10.471 --> 07:14.056
Address Tokyo Pref, Minato-Kita
History Hidamari High School
Hidamari School of Engineering

07:14.515 --> 07:15.765
He has an excellent resume.

07:15.766 --> 07:20.691
He has produced many big name TV titles,
but we don't know what he does on his days off.

07:21.233 --> 07:25.650
His graduation thesis was about explosives.

07:26.235 --> 07:29.237
Next, Yamatoya Gyo. Age 32. Unemployed.

07:26.235 --> 07:29.237
Name Yamatoya Gyo
Age 32
Occupation Unemployed

07:26.236 --> 07:29.238
Address None
History Unknown

07:29.864 --> 07:35.702
He sued the railway company, claiming that
his horse-racing ticket had been stolen.

07:36.245 --> 07:40.624
He claimed that he was headed to Osaka
that day to attend a horse race,

07:40.625 --> 07:43.543
but he did not have any train tickets in his possession.

07:44.504 --> 07:47.214
Saito Tomoyuki. Age 26. An office worker,

07:44.504 --> 07:47.214
Name Saito Tomoyuki
Age 26
Occupation Office Worker

07:44.505 --> 07:47.215
Address Tokyo Pref, Shinagawa
History Maguro University

07:47.215 --> 07:50.342
He has a pretty serious train fetish,

07:50.343 --> 07:52.886
and he admitted that he has a fairly large
grudge against the railway company

07:52.887 --> 07:55.769
for denying him employment.

07:56.265 --> 07:58.141
He served six months in the Self Defense Force,

07:58.142 --> 08:00.569
and was in the train station with a paid admission ticket.

08:01.321 --> 08:03.856
And lastly... this man...

08:04.325 --> 08:07.025
Like I said!

08:07.241 --> 08:09.694
I really must finish the story beard!

08:09.695 --> 08:11.905
Please! Let me go home!

08:12.365 --> 08:13.396
Tezuka Makoto

08:13.841 --> 08:15.010
He's a movie director.

08:15.034 --> 08:16.284
Hello?

08:16.285 --> 08:19.279
Please tell the producer that the storyboard will be late.

08:20.432 --> 08:22.373
What? Where am I now?

08:22.833 --> 08:25.426
I'm at the police station! Po-lice!

08:27.004 --> 08:28.255
What?!

08:28.256 --> 08:31.424
You don't care where I am, just draw the damn thing?!

08:33.463 --> 08:34.446
You got a problem?

08:34.770 --> 08:39.349
He was talking about bombs over the
phone right before the explosion.

08:39.350 --> 08:41.101
Was it not related to his movie?

08:41.380 --> 08:45.522
I don't care if you keep me in custody,

08:45.523 --> 08:48.984
but you should at least serve me a glass of wine.

08:48.985 --> 08:50.485
Why would I help you otherwise?

08:50.486 --> 08:54.239
You'll cooperate if I get you some wine?

08:54.320 --> 08:57.909
You see, no matter what kind of trick you pull on us,

08:57.910 --> 09:00.579
there is only one truth.

09:00.580 --> 09:03.540
Were you at the train tracks when the explosion occurred?

09:03.541 --> 09:04.749
I was.

09:04.750 --> 09:06.842
So I missed buying the ticket for the horse race.

09:07.128 --> 09:09.129
I know I would've won if I'd bought one.

09:09.130 --> 09:10.505
Answer seriously!

09:10.506 --> 09:12.048
There are many victims!

09:13.301 --> 09:17.470
People are better off dead than wasting their lives.

09:17.632 --> 09:20.932
Why were you at the train tracks
when you had no travel plans?

09:20.933 --> 09:25.270
I-I was only there to take pictures of the trains.

09:25.271 --> 09:26.563
I'm telling you the truth!

09:26.564 --> 09:28.481
I don't even have a girlfriend!

09:29.358 --> 09:31.484
I didn't ask you about that!

09:31.485 --> 09:34.988
Why did you leave the tracks right
before the train arrived?

09:34.989 --> 09:37.831
The producer was waiting on the platform.

09:38.200 --> 09:40.197
Any directer would run away in that situation.

09:40.411 --> 09:41.494
I swear.

09:41.495 --> 09:44.873
I heard you researched explosives while in school.

09:44.874 --> 09:46.875
Explosives are a man's romance.

09:46.876 --> 09:52.714
But aren't you hasty to assume I'm
the culprit just because of that?

09:52.715 --> 09:55.342
I heard you have a grudge against the railway company.

09:55.343 --> 09:56.799
I do.

09:57.219 --> 10:00.430
I nurse my grudges for a long time.

10:00.431 --> 10:02.557
Why do you like trains so much?

10:02.558 --> 10:06.523
Actually, I like the ukulele more than trains.

10:06.896 --> 10:10.732
Listen now, hiding anything from
us won't make you any richer!

10:11.734 --> 10:13.943
Well then, do you...

10:13.944 --> 10:15.278
have any proof...

10:15.279 --> 10:17.364
that I did it?!

10:23.866 --> 10:24.983
Any results, Inspector?

10:25.247 --> 10:28.458
They're all cocky and suspicious,

10:28.459 --> 10:31.032
but there's no hard evidence.

10:31.662 --> 10:34.864
I wish there was an eyewitness.

10:37.885 --> 10:40.530
But it won't be that easy.

10:41.430 --> 10:45.058
We'll have to be patient and continue gathering evidence.

10:45.601 --> 10:46.810
Right.

10:49.021 --> 10:51.523
Inspector, we found a witness.

10:51.982 --> 10:52.617
What?!

10:53.054 --> 10:54.984
She really said she saw him?

10:54.985 --> 10:55.318
Yes.

10:55.986 --> 10:58.955
The name of the witness is Mizuhara Yuko, age 23.

10:59.323 --> 11:00.793
She worked at the concession stand.

11:01.075 --> 11:05.578
She was working at the stand closest to the
scene when the explosion occurred.

11:06.381 --> 11:12.042
Her testimony is accurate and matches
the forensic findings. However...

11:27.667 --> 11:28.968
I saw him.

11:29.270 --> 11:30.895
I saw the culprit clearly.

11:31.156 --> 11:33.982
He came to the platform with a suitcase.

11:34.692 --> 11:38.611
He left the case right before the train came in,
then hurried off somewhere.

11:38.775 --> 11:41.083
That suitcase is what exploded,

11:41.657 --> 11:44.951
That's when I lost my sight.

11:44.952 --> 11:48.371
Can you describe the culprit?

11:48.372 --> 11:50.125
Describe him?

11:50.666 --> 11:53.748
He was wearing a coat and black pants.

11:54.170 --> 11:55.787
And a hat.

11:56.172 --> 11:59.132
Anything unique about his face?

11:59.925 --> 12:01.221
His face...

12:01.927 --> 12:02.955
His face...

12:05.005 --> 12:08.224
His face was pale and cold-looking.

12:09.221 --> 12:10.221
Also...

12:11.493 --> 12:12.626
Yes?

12:14.565 --> 12:15.842
I can't say it.

12:16.192 --> 12:17.633
I can't put it into words.

12:18.903 --> 12:20.874
I'll recognize him as soon as I see him.

12:21.447 --> 12:22.482
Really!

12:24.283 --> 12:27.792
Doctor! Please heal her eyes!

12:28.037 --> 12:31.164
If she could see again, we could solve this case.

12:31.165 --> 12:33.583
She's the only witness!

12:33.584 --> 12:35.168
I see.

12:35.169 --> 12:36.795
I'm sorry to hear that.

12:36.796 --> 12:37.740
You are?

12:38.339 --> 12:39.574
What do you mean?

12:39.799 --> 12:43.384
I'm sorry, but there's no way to treat her,

12:43.385 --> 12:44.856
She's...

12:45.179 --> 12:46.387
Don't tell me that.

12:47.681 --> 12:49.713
We've narrowed down the list of suspects!

12:50.059 --> 12:53.394
All we need is to let her see them,
and we can identify the culprit!

12:53.682 --> 12:56.426
You can do a transplant or whatever!

12:56.649 --> 12:59.086
Don't you have an eye bank too?

12:59.306 --> 13:00.212
Can you...

13:00.359 --> 13:05.177
The eye bank is for cornea transplants.

13:05.407 --> 13:08.883
It's impossible to transplant an entire eye.

13:09.352 --> 13:11.097
Isn't there anything you can do?

13:13.199 --> 13:14.287
I see.

13:19.755 --> 13:20.839
Inspector.

13:20.943 --> 13:21.376
Yes?

13:21.924 --> 13:24.926
There may still be a possibility.

13:24.927 --> 13:25.408
What?

13:25.912 --> 13:29.445
Maybe he can perform such a feat...

13:29.807 --> 13:32.156
A whole eye transplant.

13:33.602 --> 13:36.229
Wh-Who is this man?!

13:37.314 --> 13:40.333
He's the man with miraculous hands.

13:41.443 --> 13:43.930
Miraculous... hands?

14:07.567 --> 14:09.000
Have some tea.

14:09.014 --> 14:10.014
Thank you.

14:10.180 --> 14:11.604
A whole eye transplant, huh...

14:12.309 --> 14:17.385
I did that once in Canada, and once in France.

14:17.980 --> 14:20.138
And did you succeed?

14:20.524 --> 14:22.492
No, I failed.

14:23.819 --> 14:26.828
I used eyes from fresh corpses.

14:28.991 --> 14:30.954
But the optic nerves never worked.

14:31.744 --> 14:34.329
She seemed to regain her sight for a while.

14:34.330 --> 14:36.748
But her vision failed in five minutes.

14:36.749 --> 14:37.745
Five minutes!

14:38.083 --> 14:40.793
She could see, even for five minutes, right?!

14:42.065 --> 14:42.731
Five minutes!

14:42.755 --> 14:45.006
Even one minute will do!

14:45.007 --> 14:47.818
As long as we can show her the suspects in that time!

14:49.094 --> 14:51.080
Sure, that's fine for you.

14:51.597 --> 14:53.163
But what about the patient?

14:54.224 --> 14:57.822
She'll lose her sight again in five minutes.

15:00.508 --> 15:05.628
Sir, we surgeons perform operations to treat ailments.

15:05.945 --> 15:09.780
It's meaningless to perform an operation
when we know it will fail.

15:11.992 --> 15:13.284
There is meaning!

15:14.703 --> 15:17.523
We can arrest the culprit after identifying him.

15:17.873 --> 15:21.209
We can identify the very person who
has taken away so many lives!

15:21.210 --> 15:22.043
Don't you see?!

15:23.462 --> 15:25.922
All right, let's say that this one will be meaningful.

15:25.923 --> 15:30.922
But the patient will have to experience the
same pain a second time, just for that.

15:32.930 --> 15:36.392
You are not the one who will suffer.

15:36.850 --> 15:38.006
The patient will!

15:40.896 --> 15:43.614
You really won't do this?

15:44.149 --> 15:45.146
I refuse.

15:53.784 --> 15:55.618
Even for ¥50,000,000?

15:57.287 --> 16:01.332
¥50,000,000 is the entire budget of the department.

16:01.625 --> 16:04.535
I'll bet the entire budget on this operation!

16:05.045 --> 16:05.920
How about that?

16:11.552 --> 16:12.417
Please.

16:12.678 --> 16:15.096
I know this is a selfish request.

16:15.097 --> 16:19.737
But we can catch the culprit with your cooperation.

16:20.060 --> 16:24.485
Please help us, so we won't have
any more victims like you!

16:28.110 --> 16:29.080
All right.

16:29.945 --> 16:31.946
Th-Then...

16:31.947 --> 16:36.117
Yes, I agree to the operation.

17:25.834 --> 17:27.293
The eye is here.

17:33.675 --> 17:36.552
Will I really be able to see?

17:36.553 --> 17:39.347
Yes, although it will be for a very brief moment.

17:43.769 --> 17:46.687
We are commencing the eye transplant.

17:46.780 --> 17:48.533
In progress

18:09.459 --> 18:10.541
I'm almost finished.

18:11.130 --> 18:12.172
Bring in the suspects.

18:21.124 --> 18:22.620
Line up along the wall.

18:31.441 --> 18:33.748
Now, open your eye slowly.

18:40.325 --> 18:41.015
Well?

18:43.203 --> 18:45.196
I-I can see!

18:45.539 --> 18:46.907
I see your face!

18:47.249 --> 18:50.209
I'm sorry to rush you, but can you look this way?

18:51.974 --> 18:53.048
These are the four suspects.

18:53.297 --> 18:54.996
Look at them carefully.

18:55.299 --> 18:58.342
Is one of them the man you saw?

19:12.357 --> 19:13.524
That's the man!

19:13.525 --> 19:15.026
The second one from the right!

19:18.030 --> 19:20.281
I-I'm the culprit?!

19:20.387 --> 19:21.452
You've gotta be kidding!

19:21.742 --> 19:24.493
That's false testimony! She's lying!

19:24.620 --> 19:26.454
He put down the suitcase and fled.

19:26.662 --> 19:29.207
This is absurd. Outrageous!

19:29.208 --> 19:30.666
It's all lies!

19:30.735 --> 19:31.935
I'm sure of it!

19:32.429 --> 19:33.468
I really saw him!

19:33.889 --> 19:34.871
Now I remember.

19:35.062 --> 19:36.266
He had a mustache!

19:37.674 --> 19:43.512
Then tell me what I was wearing that day!

19:44.973 --> 19:51.187
If you make even one mistake,
it's proof that you're wrong!

19:57.635 --> 19:59.820
Take his glove off!

20:00.099 --> 20:04.450
The culprit had a cross-shaped scar
on the back of his right hand!

20:04.952 --> 20:07.161
Now, let me check.

20:07.162 --> 20:08.007
Let go of me!

20:08.205 --> 20:09.372
Stop it!

20:09.373 --> 20:10.581
Hey! What are you doing?!

20:12.542 --> 20:14.780
You can't get away from this!

20:15.504 --> 20:19.892
Suwa Michihiko! You are under arrest
for the the train station bombing!

20:28.308 --> 20:31.269
So, that closes the case.

20:32.292 --> 20:32.975
Um...

20:33.522 --> 20:34.962
I have one favor to ask.

20:35.732 --> 20:38.424
Before I lose my sight again,

20:38.819 --> 20:42.486
please take me to a place where I can see outside.

20:43.156 --> 20:46.558
I want to see outside one last time.

21:11.310 --> 21:12.383
It's so pretty!

21:13.061 --> 21:17.716
I'll never forget this scene.

21:19.151 --> 21:25.769
The beautiful town in the sunset.

21:32.748 --> 21:36.751
I'll never forget it.

21:47.139 --> 21:51.159
Choumachi Hospital

21:53.435 --> 21:58.280
Doctor, we appreciate your assistance.

21:58.565 --> 22:00.524
About the ¥50,000,000 you promised...

22:00.525 --> 22:04.612
Yes, I will personally take full responsibility
for delivering it to you.

22:04.856 --> 22:06.572
Please give it to her.

22:08.825 --> 22:10.117
You make sure of it.

22:24.104 --> 22:29.216
As you look at the ground uncertainly,

22:24.104 --> 22:29.216
tamerai gachi no fuseta hitomi

22:29.217 --> 22:34.513
I gently pull your hair closer to me.

22:29.217 --> 22:34.513
kono te ga sono kami hikiyoseteta

22:35.144 --> 22:41.645
You didn't speak, but only sighed,

22:35.144 --> 22:41.645
nani mo iezu ni kobore ochita tameiki

22:41.646 --> 22:46.108
and wet my chest with your tears.

22:41.646 --> 22:46.108
namida ga mune wo nurashita

22:46.109 --> 22:51.363
You longed to hear it, even if it was a lie.

22:46.109 --> 22:51.363
use demo ii... to kitto nozonde ita

22:51.364 --> 22:56.118
But I couldn't give you the answer you wanted.

22:51.364 --> 22:56.118
kimi no kimochi ni kotae kirezu

22:56.119 --> 23:04.543
If I gave you that answer, despite my cowardice,

22:56.119 --> 23:04.543
okubyou na boku ga moshi sono toki kotaetetara mada

23:04.544 --> 23:08.130
would we still be together?

23:04.544 --> 23:08.130
tsuzuiteita noka?

23:08.131 --> 23:13.427
That irregular breath my body was accustomed to,

23:08.131 --> 23:13.427
karada ga oboeta fukisoku na breath

23:13.431 --> 23:18.891
I want to feel it one more time.

23:13.431 --> 23:18.891
mou ichido subete de kanjitai

23:18.892 --> 23:24.396
The breath of surprise when I lost everything.

23:18.892 --> 23:24.396
subete wo nakushita fuyoui na breath

23:24.397 --> 23:33.572
And the pain that binds me every time I feel regret.

23:24.397 --> 23:33.572
kuyamu tabi mata sono itami ga shimetsukeru

23:45.059 --> 24:15.022
Crib in the Locker

23:46.146 --> 23:47.746
A lullaby by a delinquent girl.

23:48.026 --> 23:52.884
It's the sorrowful ballad of a small
abandoned life and the girl who saves it.

23:53.814 --> 23:54.126
Are you...

23:54.166 --> 23:54.906
Shut the hell up!

23:55.426 --> 23:58.445
Neither Daddy nor Mom care about me.

24:00.346 --> 24:01.106
Damn it!

24:02.006 --> 24:03.166
He's suffering from severe malnutrition.

24:03.366 --> 24:04.129
Please save him!

24:04.429 --> 24:05.617
Why are you so desperate to save him?

24:05.684 --> 24:08.569
Some day I'm going to leave home
and live alone with hin.

24:08.697 --> 24:10.910
Ohmibaby!

24:11.124 --> 24:14.558
Black Jack, Next Karte - Crib in the Locker.

24:15.600 --> 24:17.351
Karte NG...

24:18.328 --> 24:19.068
Second from...

24:19.312 --> 24:20.562
Huh?

24:21.564 --> 24:22.793
Who the heck are you?!

24:23.023 --> 24:24.600
Oh, you don't need me?
